1. U-04, WHAT THE REQUIREMENTS DEMAND OF SOURCE-ONLY OPERATION (quoted, not reinterpreted)
   REQ-015 statement: "A 9 to 36 V vehicle and shore input runs the kit and charges the pack, with reverse-polarity protection, under- and over-voltage limits, a line filter designed to MIL-STD-461 limits, a NATO 2-pin plug cable and the MIL-DTL-38999 receptacle. The input is not qualified against any vehicle surge standard and is not intended for 24 V military vehicle buses (D-16)." (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-015 acceptance: "Operates and charges across 9 to 36 V, and takes a reversed input and an over-voltage to the front end's limit (40 V, 32.55) without damage, on the prototype; CE102 under its limit line (TEST-PLAN M1)." (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-014: "missions longer than the pack rely on vehicle or solar input (D-06)" (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-024: "a pack cold-soaked below about -10 C at the cells is not started from (shore or vehicle power, or warming, first; D-02d)" (REQUIREMENT)
   TEST-PLAN E4-O (REQ-024's acceptance): "started warm or from shore or vehicle input (D-02d: a cold start from the pack below about -10 C cell temperature is out of scope; inside the envelope, so an acceptance test)" (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-046: "The cells are charged only between 0 and +45 C and discharged only between -10 and +60 C at the cell surface; below 0 C the pack is warmed by its heater mat before charge."; its acceptance: "the bridge's own hold clears above 3 C (PANEL.md section 10)" (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-077 acceptance: "the charge held by the charger's CHRG_INHIBIT with the charger still carrying the kit on shore" (REQUIREMENT)
   REQ-072 (obligation OBJECTIVE): "after a permitted pack cutoff the remaining supply carries the loads, D-26" (REQUIREMENT)
   requirement | obligation | source voltage named | names a load state | the source-only content
     REQ-015          | MANDATORY | 9 to 36 V, where measured not stated | no | operates and charges; the pack's state not named (REQUIREMENT)
     REQ-014          | MANDATORY | none | no | missions longer than the pack rely on vehicle or solar input (REQUIREMENT)
     REQ-024 (D-02d)  | MANDATORY | shore or vehicle (9 to 36 V by REQ-015) | no | a cold-soaked pack: both FETs open below -9 C, the kit started on the source (REQUIREMENT)
     REQ-046          | MANDATORY | none | no | below 0 C the pack warmed by its heater before charge; the bridge's hold clears above 3 C (REQUIREMENT)
     REQ-077          | MANDATORY | on shore | no | the charge held by CHRG_INHIBIT while the charger carries the kit (a pack present) (REQUIREMENT)
     REQ-072          | OBJECTIVE | solar | yes | after a permitted pack cutoff the remaining supply carries the loads (PS-IDLE-SPEC is the objective's profile) (REQUIREMENT)
   So: no mandatory requirement names a load state (a PS- profile or a wattage) for the kit on a source alone, at any
     source voltage; REQ-015's "runs the kit and charges the pack" names neither the load nor the pack's state, and "9 V"
     is not tied to a measuring point. PS-IDLE-SPEC enters only through REQ-072, an objective. What the mandatory text does
     demand of a source alone: a start and a warm-up of a cold-soaked pack whose FETs are open (REQ-024, D-02d, REQ-046,
     E4-O), and the charger carrying the kit with its charge held (REQ-077, a pack present). (INFERRED from the quotes)

2. U-04, THE CHARGER AND THE PACK WITH NO USABLE PACK
   BQ25731 (SLUSE66A), what the sheet states:
     no battery MOSFET (p.1); from VBUS: registers, cell count, then "Converter powers up." with no battery condition (9.3.1, p.24) (MAKER)
     power-up curves drawn "2-cell without battery", Figures 10-4 and 10-5 (p.89) (MAKER)
     "When CHRG_OK goes HIGH, the system is powered from adapter through the charger. When adapter is removed, the system is connected to battery." (11, p.92) (MAKER)
     CHRG_OK's conditions name VBUS and the faults, not the battery: "VBUS is above VVBUS_CONVEN VBUS is below VACOV_FALL No faults triggered such as: SYSOVP/SYSUVP/ACOC/TSHUT/BATOVP/BATOC/force converter off." (9.3.4, p.25) (MAKER)
     DPM: the charge falls first, then "the system voltage starts to drop" and the battery supplements (9.3.17, p.29) (MAKER)
     4S defaults: ChargeVoltage 16.8 V, SYSOVP 19.5 V, VSYS_MIN 12.3 V (Table 9-2, p.26); below VSYS_MIN at SRN the charge is clamped at 384 mA, a typical figure with no minimum or maximum printed (8.5, p.10) (MAKER)
     in the BATOVP paragraph: with charge enabled the converter shuts down; "if charge is disabled the converter should keep operating without disturbance"
       (9.3.21.5, p.34): a statement about a battery over-voltage event, not a specification of VSYS's regulation or transient response with no battery (N1, N2) (MAKER, context kept)
     HIZ: "converter shuts off" with ILIM_HIZ under 0.4 V (9.3.8, p.26) (MAKER)
     VSYS under 1.6 V for 2 ms in steady state: "shut down and latched off" until a host write (9.3.21.8, p.34) (MAKER)
     "Overall 50-uF effective capacitance on VSYS net is necessary" (10.1, p.83); CHRG_INHIBIT "1b: Inhibit Charge" (p.44); the host ends a charge by CHRG_INHIBIT or ChargeCurrent 0 (9.4.1, p.35) (MAKER)
     AUTO_WAKEUP_EN, 0 at POR: with it set, a battery under VSYS_MIN gets 128 mA for 30 min with no further host write (p.61) (MAKER); it needs a host write first, so it does not answer N3
     ChargeCurrent at POR: the register description says 0 A, its reset value encodes 256 mA, and TI's expert on E2E thread 1316778 (held) states 256 mA,
       the description being in error (the dependency round, D4) (MAKER)
     ChargeCurrent with the 5 mOhm RSR: 128 mA steps; REG0x03/02 = 0x0200 (1024 mA) regulates within -18 % to +21.5 %, a row printed for VBAT above VSYS_MIN (8.5, p.10) (MAKER)
   board A and E as generated: the strap R26 13.3k over R27 40.2k, 75.1 % of VDDA, so U3 never sees "battery removal"; R17 between VBAT
     (VSYS, every load) and CELL_FUSED (the pack); CHG_INHIBIT pulls ILIM_HIZ low through Q6 (HIZ); SHORE_INHIBIT pulls the hot
     swap's UVLO low through Q8 (the input off); board P's gauge PCHG pin not connected; R7 1 k from PACK_P to its VCC (NETLIST)
     FW-C08 as written: "Boot low. Asserted only on the operator's 'inputs off' and on the water-on-floor isolation, never for a temperature or 'no charge' hold (those are FW-A19's flag and the charger's CHRG_INHIBIT bit). When the pack cannot discharge (states S2 and S4: the gauge's XDSG, no pack, or both FETs open) the bridge first warns that asserting it removes the kit's supply (L4-E11 7a, rule R-a; LH-10)" (RECORD, HW-FW-CONTRACT)
     FW-A14 as written: "Held low (charger enabled) at power-up; asserted only by firmware, never as a charge hold (a hold is the CHRG_INHIBIT bit or ChargeCurrent 0, FW-A19), and never while the pack cannot discharge (S2, S4: HIZ stops the converter and removes the kit's only supply) (L4-E11 7a; LH-10)" (RECORD); PANEL.md 10: "high = the shore and vehicle inputs are held off at the front end, so nothing charges." (RECORD)
   the pack (SLUUAQ3A and this tree's image):
     a CUV trip sets OperationStatus()[XDSG] only (2.2, p.15): the discharge FET opens, the charge FET stays (MAKER)
     XDSG also on UTD, XCHG on UTC (4.12, p.40); the image's UTD -9 C and UTC 1 C (pcb_pack_protection.yaml): below -9 C both FETs are open (MAKER, RECORD)
     precharge by the external FET or the CHG FET per PCHG_COMM (4.9, p.38), default 0 = PCHG FET (14.2.1.1, p.117); board P has no PCHG FET and
     the image writes FET Options 0x3D, PCHG_COMM 1 (PRIMARY-CONFIGURATION.md); Shutdown Voltage 2000 mV; CUV 2.5 V, recovery 3 V; pre-charge 1 A (MAKER, RECORD)
     Q2's body diode carries the charge while XDSG: VSD at most 1 V at 50 A, RthetaJA at most 50 C/W on 1 in2 2 oz, TJ 150 C (CSD17570Q5B p.3) (MAKER)
       at 0.384 A: at most 0.384 W, 19.2 K over the air (INFERRED: VSD's row at 50 A bounds it at less current; board P's copper an ASSUMPTION)
       at 3 A: at most 3 W, 150 K over the air (INFERRED: VSD's row at 50 A bounds it at less current; board P's copper an ASSUMPTION)
       at R-b's 1.257 A (below): at most 1.257 W, 62.8 K, so TJ 124.9 C at the 62.1 C inside air against 150 C (CONDITIONAL: on R-b's bound holding, below, and
         on board P's installed copper giving TI's 50 C/W, which TI states for its own 1 in2 2 oz board; INFERRED)
     the cell maker: pre-charge between 1 and 3 V a cell at 0.1 to 0.5 C, C = 3.4 A (Samsung 35E p.14) (MAKER); the charger's 384 mA is 0.038 C a cell,
       under the range (a lower current; the maker states no consequence), and a 3.0 A ChargeCurrent is 0.294 C a cell, inside it (INFERRED)
   what follows, by pack state (INFERRED from the rows above, the drawn topology and the image):
     pack absent, or both FETs open (below -9 C, SHUTDOWN, a permanent fail): no current through R17, so the voltage loop holds
       SRN, and VSYS with it, at ChargeVoltage (at most 16.884 V written, s120); the kit is carried up to the input limit (11, 9.3.17) (INFERRED)
     pack at CUV, charge FET on: charge through Q2's diode; VSYS = stack + VSD, 10 to 11 V; 384 mA while SRN is under 12.3 V (CONDITIONAL on A-14's 10.0 V floor)
     a pack self-discharged to the Shutdown Voltage: VSYS 8 to 9 V while it precharges, under the converters' assumed 10.0 V floor (A-14): the loads wait (CONDITIONAL)
     the clamp lifts at SRN 12.3 V, a stack of 11.3 V or more (2.825 V a cell) with VSD at its maximum, before CUV recovers at 3 V a cell: in that window
       ChargeCurrent crosses Q2's diode, so rule R-b (SESSION) permits exactly two settings while the charger's own SRN reading is under 14 V or the
       gauge reports XDSG or PRECHARGE: ChargeCurrent() 0x0000 (no charge) and 0x0200 (1024 mA set); no other value, because TI prints no accuracy
       for any setting under 0x0200 (MAKER, SESSION). The bounds by case (B5; the row's condition: 5 mOhm RSR, VBAT above VSYS_MIN, 0 to 85 C):
       (i) SRN at or above VSYS_MIN and the charger inside 0 to 85 C: 0.8314 to 1.2567 A actual (-18 / +21.5 %, R17 at +-1 %) (MAKER row, INFERRED: BOUNDED)
       (ii) SRN at or above VSYS_MIN with the charger outside 0 to 85 C: no accuracy printed: INCONCLUSIVE until the charger's temperature in this
            state is bounded inside the row (it sits in the inside air, -20 C at a cold start to 62.1 C hot, plus its own rise, which no held record gives),
            or TI states the accuracy outside it, or the bench measures the current at the inside air's ends (E11-22)
       (iii) SRN under VSYS_MIN: the clamp, 384 mA typical with no maximum printed: INCONCLUSIVE until TI states a maximum or the bench measures it (E11-22)
       without the gauge's report the 14 V threshold covers a cell up to 0.25 V under the stack's average (3.25 V a cell) (INFERRED); R-b also holds above 14 V
       while the gauge reports XDSG or PRECHARGE, so in case (i) the charge power is at most 1.2567 A x 16.884 V = 21.22 W (at the 14 V threshold, 17.59 W) (INFERRED)
     CHG_INHIBIT (HIZ) or SHORE_INHIBIT asserted while the pack cannot discharge: the converter is off, so VSYS has no source and the
       kit stops; the controllers die, the pull-downs release the line and the kit restarts: a loop (INFERRED: 9.3.8, the UVLO, the netlists)
     FW-C08 asserts SHORE_INHIBIT below 0 C: with a pack below -9 C the source start REQ-024 requires is cut by the hold itself (finding U4-F1, INFERRED)
   NOT STATED in any held document (named, not inferred): N1 VSYS's regulation and transient response with no battery under the
     kit's load steps; N2 what the converter regulates with CHRG_INHIBIT = 1 or ChargeCurrent 0 and no battery current (Q-TI-3);
     N3 whether the charger charges before any host write (Q-TI-2); N4 VSYS's effective capacitance at 16.884 V against TI's 50 uF (RECORD, MAKER);
     N5 every load converter's minimum input (A-14, R-49); N6 0-V charging before the gauge's SUV check (Q-TI-7)
   THE PACK'S STATES BY PERMISSION (B2; the gauge's own FETs, SLUUAQ3A 2.2 and 4.12) and how a charge hold is made in each (INFERRED):
     S1 charge on, discharge on: the pack and the source share the kit; a hold by the CHRG_INHIBIT bit or ChargeCurrent 0 (9.4.1) leaves the converter
        carrying the kit from the source (11): REQ-077 as written
     S2 charge on, discharge off (a warm CUV trip, or an OCD, AOLD or SCD latch): the source alone carries the kit and the pack can still take charge
        through Q2's diode, so the gauge does NOT hold the charge; a hold only by the bit or ChargeCurrent 0; whether VSYS stays regulated with charge
        inhibited while the pack cannot discharge is N2 (Q-TI-3): OPEN, the bench proves it (E11-06)
     S3 charge off, discharge on (between UTD -9 C and UTC 1 C; OTC; COV): the gauge holds the charge; a requested hold by the bit as in S1 (REQ-077)
     S4 charge off, discharge off (below -9 C, SHUTDOWN, a permanent fail, or no pack): the source alone carries the kit and the gauge already holds
        the charge. THE ONE EXCEPTION: in S4 the bit is NOT set and ChargeCurrent() is not written 0, so N2 never arises where the source alone carries
        the kit with no charge possible; the hold is the gauge's own
     THE HOLD PERSISTS ACROSS STATES: it is a flag in the firmware, set and cleared only by its own condition (the cold hold above 3 C with hysteresis,
        the operator, REQ-077's hold), never by a state change; in S1, S2 and S3 the bit follows the flag; on leaving S4 (a FET closing, a pack fitted)
        the bit is written from the flag at once, and in the firmware's reaction time only the gauge's window acts, which keeps the cells inside their
        charge window; after a charger POR ChargeCurrent() is 256 mA by TI's E2E answer (D4), so a charge at 256 mA can begin before the firmware writes the
        flag's bit: in that window too only the gauge's window acts, and 256 mA is under R-b's bound (INFERRED)
     in S2 and S4 the CHG_INHIBIT line (HIZ, 9.3.8) and SHORE_INHIBIT each remove the kit's only supply: neither is ever a charge hold (rule R-a)

