5. U-04, IS AN OWNER QUESTION FORCED?
   a mandatory requirement naming a load state for source-only operation: none (section 1); the warm-up sequence of 3g is carried at its plan figure
   what the source path itself admits at a 9.00 V plug, the kit's losses included and VBUS20's other loads taken off (INFERRED; the first round's
     59.5 / 79.8 / 89.6 W left the losses out):
     F1's 80 C column, 7.3 A, the losses hot        142.34 mOhm: VIN_RAW 7.961 V, 50.99 W at VBAT (MAKER, INFERRED)
     F1's 0 C column, 9.8 A, the losses cold        97.71 mOhm: VIN_RAW 8.042 V, 69.73 W at VBAT (MAKER, INFERRED)
     a 15 A MINI's 80 C column, 11 A, the losses hot 142.34 mOhm: VIN_RAW 7.434 V, 72.41 W at VBAT (MAKER, INFERRED)
     (the check's reference, 115.511 mOhm with no auxiliary load: 7.3 A 53.9 W, 9.8 A 69.79 W, 11 A 76.96 W)
   these are the path's ceilings with the electronics set to use all of them; the breaker's band and the knee's spread keep the least delivered
     figure lower (3h: 29.09 W at 9 V) (INFERRED). REQ-015 states no source current capability: every figure takes the source as holding its voltage (named)
   so NO owner question is forced: no approved requirement names a load REQ-015's 9 V must carry beyond the functional sequence, which 3c to 3g carry at
     its plan figure (CONDITIONAL, 3g). Against the ceilings: PS-TYP 63 W is over F1's hot ceiling 50.99 W and under its cold 69.73 W; the CONOPS cold warm-up
     71.06 W (a cold state, so F1's cold column applies) is over its cold ceiling 69.73 W; a 15 A part's hot ceiling 72.41 W is over both. So the kit at 9 V with F1 as
     fitted does not carry PS-TYP hot or the CONOPS warm-up cold: a design envelope stated, not a conflict with an approved requirement (INFERRED)

