9. THE DEPENDENCY ROUND: EACH MISSING SPECIFICATION, THE CLAIM IT DECIDES, WHO CAN SETTLE IT (2 October 2026)
   the held answer on the POR value: TI's expert on E2E thread 1316778: "The POR value is indeed 256mA" (the register description's 0 A is in error) (MAKER, forum)
   D1 N1a, VSYS's DC regulation with no battery (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: no row gives VSYS's regulation with no battery current: VBAT_REG_ACC +-0.5 % holds for a charge voltage at 0 to 85 C (p.9); section 11 (p.92) says the system is powered through the charger; Figures 10-4 and 10-5 (p.89) are typical power-up curves of a 2-cell system without battery
     the claim: section 2's row 'absent, or both FETs open: VSYS at ChargeVoltage' and every S4 figure of 3g and 3h (U-04 in S4 at all)
     a maker's answer would establish: that the voltage loop holds VSYS at ChargeVoltage with no battery current, with the +-0.5 % row applying: production-wide if TI states it as a limit
     a bench sample could establish: that one unit enters and holds the mode at the conditions tried; the mode is a design behaviour, and VSYS needs only 12.3 V against ChargeVoltage's floor 16.716 V, a 4.416 V margin that is large against any plausible unit spread once the mode is shown (an engineering margin)
     a bench sample cannot establish: that every unit and silicon revision enters the mode, or the accuracy below 0 C, where the +-0.5 % row stops
     the bench method: pack absent, P1's load and the envelope's maximum on VSYS, VBUS20 from 19.1 to 21 V, VSYS on a calibrated meter at -20, 25 and 62 C ambient
     if the answer is negative: arrangement (A) does not run S4: (B), a charger with a battery FET that regulates VSYS by design (an architecture change; five records reopen)
   D2 N1b, VSYS's load-step response with no battery (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: no load-transient figure or limit for the system output (Figure 10-17, p.91, is the OTG output's)
     the claim: S4 operation through the kit's load steps (3g, R-c): the declared steps of section 10, up to 48.39 W
     a maker's answer would establish: a characterised deviation and recovery, or a minimum loop bandwidth; production-wide only if TI states a limit
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's deviation and recovery at the steps tried; with the bank sized for 1 ms, a measured recovery of 0.2 ms or less is a five-fold margin, large against a loop's plausible spread (L, C and gain tolerances): an engineering margin
     a bench sample cannot establish: a recovery time bounded for every unit
     the bench method: pack absent, an electronic load stepping VSYS by each declared step with a 1 us edge, VSYS and the inductor current on a scope, at the three ambients
     if the answer is negative: the bank of section 10 carries the step for 1.117 ms with no help from the charger; a longer recovery needs more cans (8 for 2 ms) or (B)
   D3 N2 (Q-TI-3), VSYS with CHRG_INHIBIT = 1 or ChargeCurrent 0 and no battery current (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: 9.4.1 (p.35) lets the host end a charge by CHRG_INHIBIT or ChargeCurrent 0; 9.3.21.5 (p.34) keeps the converter operating with charge disabled only in the BATOVP paragraph; nothing states what VSYS does in either state with no battery current
     the claim: R-a's S2 row and REQ-077's hold in every state (section 4): the charger still carrying the kit while the charge is held
     a maker's answer would establish: the control mode with charge inhibited, production-wide (a design behaviour)
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's mode with the bit set and with ChargeCurrent 0, pack absent and in S2: a deterministic logic behaviour, so one sample is strong evidence for that silicon revision
     a bench sample cannot establish: that no later revision changes the mode, nor how a temperature-dependent comparator moves it
     the bench method: the pack emulated in S2 (a supply behind a diode), the bit set and cleared under P1's load, VSYS and the switch node recorded
     if the answer is negative: REQ-077's hold cannot use the bit with this charger; ChargeCurrent 0 is tried; if both fail, (B) or a requirement change to REQ-077's acceptance (the owner's)
   D4 N3 (Q-TI-2), whether the charger charges before any host write (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: 9.6.3 says the charge starts when the host writes ChargeCurrent(); the register's reset value encodes 256 mA and its description says 0 A at POR. TI's expert on E2E thread 1316778 (held) answers: the POR value is 256 mA, the description is in error; 9.6.3 is not addressed
     the claim: section 2's ChargeCurrent at POR (corrected in this round), R-a's persistence after a charger POR, CONOPS's hostless 256 mA
     a maker's answer would establish: a datasheet erratum: production-wide (a forum answer is TI's word but not a revised document)
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's SRP-SRN current after POR with no host: a logic behaviour, strong for that revision
     a bench sample cannot establish: other revisions
     the bench method: no host, the pack at 3.6 V a cell, the SRP-SRN current read for 200 s after POR
     if the answer is negative: a hostless charge at 256 mA is safe (inside the gauge's window; Q2's diode 0.256 W); no hostless charge leaves a hostless kit's dead pack uncharged: a stated limitation, no change
   D5 N4, VSYS's effective capacitance at 16.884 V against TI's 50 uF (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: TI states 50 uF effective necessary (10.1, p.83); the fitted MLCCs' capacitance at 16.9 V of DC bias is not printed in the held Yageo CC sheet (a capacitor maker's item, not TI's)
     the claim: N1's premise (stable regulation) and E11-07
     a maker's answer would establish: the capacitor makers' DC-bias curves: typical per part number, not limits
     a bench sample could establish: one board's VSYS capacitance at 16.8 V of bias: a sample
     a bench sample cannot establish: lot-to-lot spread
     the bench method: an LCR meter with DC bias on the populated node, or each part number on a bias fixture
     if the answer is negative: none needed: one EEHZK1V181P on VSYS gives 90.72 uF at its stacked worst, with no DC-bias dependence, over 50 uF by design
   D6 Q-TI-7, 0-V charging before the gauge's SUV check (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: SLUUAQ3A 4.9: with PCHG_COMM = 1 the hardware 0-V charging circuit is enabled below the minimum operation voltage; nothing states its timing against the SUV check of 3.2.1
     the claim: R-d (the image keeps PCHG_COMM 1 and the SUV check): no cell below 1.0 V charged (Samsung)
     a maker's answer would establish: the gauge's sequence, production-wide
     a bench sample could establish: one gauge with a cell simulator: a logic sequence, strong for that firmware and revision
     a bench sample cannot establish: other firmware revisions
     the bench method: a cell simulator at 0.8 V a cell, the charger enabled, the stack current logged from the gauge's wake
     if the answer is negative: ZVCHG Exit Threshold set to stop 0-V charging, or a precharge FET (arrangement (C)'s part) with PCHG_COMM 0
   D7 the clamp's maximum under VSYS_MIN (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: 8.5 (p.10) prints the clamp under VSYS_MIN, 384 mA, as typical only
     the claim: R-b's case (iii) and Q2's diode below VSYS_MIN (section 4)
     a maker's answer would establish: a maximum, production-wide
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's clamp current; Q2 reaches 150 C only at 1.758 A on its 50 C/W, 4.58 times the typical clamp, so a sample near typical is a large engineering margin
     a bench sample cannot establish: a maximum for every unit
     the bench method: SRN held at 11 V by a sink, ChargeCurrent 0x0200, the current read at -20, 25 and 62 C
     if the answer is negative: a maximum over 1.758 A: Q2's copper improved, or arrangement (C)
   D8 ChargeCurrent's accuracy at 0x0200 outside 0 to 85 C, and under 0x0200 (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: p.10's rows hold for VBAT above VSYS_MIN at 0 to 85 C; no accuracy outside that range, nor for any setting under 0x0200
     the claim: R-b's case (ii) and Q2's 124.9 C (section 4, CONDITIONAL)
     a maker's answer would establish: limits outside the range, production-wide
     a bench sample could establish: one unit at -20 and 62 C ambient: a sample; Q2's limit 1.758 A is 1.4 times R-b's 1.2567 A, so a sample within about 1.3 A is an engineering margin
     a bench sample cannot establish: production limits
     the bench method: as D7 with SRN at 13 V
     if the answer is negative: the charger's temperature bounded inside the row by layout (E11-22), or Q2's copper improved
   D9 the TPS48110-Q1's overcurrent delay at CTMR 22 nF (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: SLUSEE5E p.10 prints 370 us typical only
     the claim: V-A08's 0.247 ms (the nuisance margin) and the fault scan's 0.49 ms (A11-11)
     a maker's answer would establish: a minimum and a maximum over temperature, production-wide
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's delay: a sample; the scan's worst fault ends on the short-circuit trip (3c), so the delay's maximum does not decide it; its minimum sets V-A08
     a bench sample cannot establish: the spread across units
     the bench method: a current step over the threshold at three temperatures, the sense step to PD timed
     if the answer is negative: V-A08's allowance re-derived on TI's minimum, or CTMR raised
   D10 the CSD19536KTT's transconductance bound (MAKER, INFERRED)
     missing: SLPS540C p.3 prints gfs 329 S typical only
     the claim: the start into a hard short (3c, 0.743 of the derated chart)
     a maker's answer would establish: a maximum, or the transfer curve's spread
     a bench sample could establish: one unit's transfer curve; the headroom (1.346 times) is not large against a plausible transconductance spread, so a sample is no margin
     a bench sample cannot establish: a bound across units
     the bench method: a pulsed transfer curve at VDS 10 V, 10 to 100 A
     if the answer is negative: a slower gate slew for the start (C1 larger) or a power-limiting controller

10. THE BOUNDED FALLBACK (E11-07, VSYS's capacitance first): A HOLD-UP THAT DOES NOT LEAN ON THE CHARGER'S TRANSIENT RESPONSE
   the criterion: with no battery (S4) VSYS sits at ChargeVoltage, at least 16.716 V (16.8 V less TI's 0.5 %, p.9, MAKER), and must stay above VSYS_MIN 12.3 V
