       returns it to 0 A and a non-zero write resumes the charge (p.36); VSYS_MIN becomes a register, 12.3 V at POR for 4S (p.83); EN_LDO 1,
       EN_PORT_CTRL 1, BATFET_ENZ 0 and BATFETOFF_HIZ 0 at POR (pp.48, 67, 68): the BATFET driven, on in HIZ; EN_OOA 1 at POR (p.47); the device
       ID reads D5h, not D6h; I2C address 6Bh the same (MAKER)
   12c. THE THREE MODES: THE STATEMENT THAT BOUNDS VSYS IN EACH (the acceptance)
     the table's conditions: TJ -40 to 125 C unless a row says otherwise (p.9); the two VSYS rows hold "OOA disabled", and EN_OOA is 1 at POR,
       so the firmware writes EN_OOA 0 at boot for the printed accuracy to apply (SESSION; before that the modes are stated, their accuracy not) (MAKER)
     (1) battery present, the source on: p.38, "system voltage is regulated 150 mV above battery voltage when BATFET is turned off", the BATFET
       fully on while charging or supplementing, VSYS_MIN the floor; VSYS from 12.054 V (the floor), or, with the source overloaded, the pack less
       Q39's drop as it supplements (9.786 V at the CUV stack and OCD1's 20 A, 12e, as (A)'s pack sits on VSYS less R17's drop),
       to 17.375 V (the pack at ChargeVoltage's 16.884 V plus 150 mV, +2 %, p.9): BOUNDED (MAKER, INFERRED)
       startup: from VBUS the registers, the cell count from CELL_BATPRESZ, then "Converter powers up" (p.27); with only the battery, above
       VVBAT_UVLOZ (2.35 to 2.8 V on SRN), "charger wakes up and the BATFET is turned on" (p.27); no charge until ChargeCurrent is written (p.49) (MAKER)
     (2) battery absent (or both of the pack's FETs open), the source on: p.1's instant-on; p.38, below VSYS_MIN "the BATFET operates in linear
       mode (LDO mode), and the system is regulated at VSYS_MIN"; VSYS_MIN_REG_ACC 12.3 V, minimum -2 % (p.10): at least 12.054 V at TJ -40 to 125 C;
       at most 17.375 V by the VSYS pin's maximum limit and VSYSMAX_ACC (p.7, p.9): BOUNDED (MAKER, INFERRED)
       the exact gap: VSYS_MIN_REG_ACC prints -2 % in its maximum column as well (p.10), so the row's upper side is not printed; no claim here rests on it
       (the floor decides every claim); where a figure needs it, 12.546 V is taken (+2 %, ASSUMPTION) (MAKER)
       startup: the same power-up from VBUS (p.27); VSYS_UVP clamps the input to 0.5 A while VSYS is under 2.4 V and, after 2 ms, shuts the
       converter for 500 ms and retries for 10 ms, latching after 7 failures in 90 s (p.38) (MAKER); VSYS's capacitance at most 489 uF (the VBAT net's
       248.2 uF of ceramics plus 10 %, and the direct can at +20 %); WITHDRAWN by the fix round: the 0.5 A is the input clamp, not a delivered
       current, so no start time follows from it; the start is bounded in 15b (INFERRED)
     (3) battery present, charging inhibited: CHRG_INHIBIT 1 inhibits the charge (p.48); VSYSMAX_ACC with charge disabled: VSRN + 150 mV within
       +-2 % (p.9), the BATFET off, so no battery current unless the load exceeds the source (supplement, p.5); with the pack at its CUV stack VSYS
       is at least 12.054 V: BOUNDED (MAKER, INFERRED); startup as (1), the bit at 0 by POR, written from the hold flag (section 14)
     so each mode has the maker's printed bound on VSYS (D1 and D3 removed); the margin from the floor to A-14's assumed 10.0 V converter floor:
       2.054 V, which a load step in S2 or S4 must not use up (D2, no transient limit printed) (INFERRED)
   12d. PROTECTION (MAKER)
     the input, system and battery over-voltage, input over-current, converter OCP and thermal rows are the same (12b); VSYS_UVP moves to 2.4 V with
       hiccup (12c); BATOC stops the converter and "BATFET status is not impacted if need to supplement power to system" (p.37); in HIZ the BATFET
       stays on (BATFETOFF_HIZ 0), so CHG_INHIBIT's HIZ leaves the kit on the pack exactly as with the BQ25731 (R-a's rule on the line holds);
       BATFET_ENZ would force the BATFET off on battery and the kit would run through its body diode: never written (SESSION)
