16. THE FIX ROUND FOR THE REVIEW OF THE PROVISIONAL FIXES (L4-F02 and L4-F03; a qualification gap, not a demonstrated failure)
   16a. L4-F02 OBJECTION 1: RDS(on) AT BATDRV'S LEAST DRIVE (BATDRV 8.5 / 10 / 11.5 V, SLUSE65A p.17; the source on VSYS, so VGS is minus that)
     printed by the BUK6Y10-30P (17 April 2020, Table 7, p.6): at most 10 mOhm at -10 V and 25 C, 16 mOhm at -10 V and 175 C, 25 mOhm at -4.5 V
       and 25 C; no maximum at a gate drive under 10 V above 25 C, so no printed point bounds the operating point (-8.5 V, hot) (MAKER)
     the 21.136 mOhm of 15c is WITHDRAWN AS A BOUND: it is kept as the ALLOWANCE each FET is sized to (SESSION), and E11-36 confirms it on
       parts (RDS(on) at -8.5 V and 150 C, at most 21.136 mOhm) or reverses it; at the sheet's largest printed maximum, 25 mOhm, every figure below
       scales by 1.1828 (printed beside it); parts at 25 mOhm on a board built to the allowance would take 20 A held to 152.8 C and the service to
       137.1 C, so E11-36 gates E11-29 (SESSION, CONDITIONAL)
     searched: SQJ403EP (held), AONS21357 (held), SQJ407EP (Vishay 62806 Rev. B, filed held) and PXP9R1-30QL (Nexperia, 5 January 2021, filed
       held) print their hot maxima at -10 V only; no part read prints one at |VGS| of 8.5 V or less above 25 C (MAKER)
     STATUS: CONDITIONAL on E11-36 (the measurement, or Nexperia's maximum at the point, filed) (SESSION)
   16b. L4-F02 OBJECTION 2: THE DEVICE'S OWN TRANSIENT IMPEDANCE AND THE TWO FETS' COUPLING
     Fig. 4 (p.5), the duty-cycle 0.01 curve (above any single pulse), read on the rendered page (inputs/nexperia-buk6y10-30p-figure-readings-2026-10-02.json): its plateau 1.3225 K/W, scaled by
       1.0586 to Table 6's maximum Rth(j-mb) 1.4 K/W: Zth(j-mb) 0.2589 K/W at 244 us, 1.3571 at 20 ms, 1.4 at 1 s, 1.4 at 60 s (MAKER, read; INFERRED scale)
     AOS's Figure 14 shape is no longer used for these FETs. The installed path is stated as what a bench reads: each FET's self impedance
       Zself(t) (heat one, read its own junction) and the mutual Zmut(t) (heat one, read the other); then for any split of the pair's current
       TJ <= air + Pb x (Zself + Zmut)(t), Pb the even split's per-FET power at the allowance (it bounds each FET's power, 15c); Zself includes
       the device's own Zth(j-mb); the coupling is in the sum, not assumed away (INFERRED)
     the plan at the +70 C mixed air (SESSION): 20 A held under OCD1 reaches 140 C at most (10 K under the 150 C limit kept for the pulses), so
       the installed (Zself + Zmut) at steady state at most 33.12 K/W (28 at 25 mOhm); per-FET power 0.5284 W at 10 A, 1.712 W at 18 A, 2.1136 W at 20 A (INFERRED)
     THE SERVICE, 18 A FOR 60 S FROM THE HOT STATE (10 A held at the +70 C air, no board capacity credited, so 60 s counts as steady): TJ 126.7 C,
       from 87.5 C at 10 A held, 23.3 K under the limit; the 18 A for 60 s is kept and no protection is lowered (INFERRED, CONDITIONAL on E11-29, E11-36)
     the fault histories from the held 20 A (each a step from the 140 C ceiling to the 150 C limit): the allowance on the installed sum at the
       event's width, against the device's own Zth(j-mb) at that width (INFERRED):
       OCD2 24 A for 1 s: per FET 3.044 W; (Zself + Zmut) at 1 s at most 10.753 K/W (9.091 at 25 mOhm), the device alone 1.4 K/W, so 9.353 K/W for the board and the coupling
       AOLD 30 A for 20 ms: per FET 4.756 W; (Zself + Zmut) at 0.02 s at most 3.785 K/W (3.2 at 25 mOhm), the device alone 1.3571 K/W, so 2.428 K/W for the board and the coupling
       ASCD 55.6 A for 244 us: per FET 16.335 W; (Zself + Zmut) at 0.000244 s at most 0.703 K/W (0.594 at 25 mOhm), the device alone 0.2589 K/W, so 0.444 K/W for the board and the coupling
     the LDO-mode precharge, one FET linear with 0.33616 A: under the plan's steady sum it stays at 150 C down to SRN 5.36 V, so R-b' (no charge under
       5.7 V) keeps its margin (INFERRED)
