       channel 1 (OV) reads EF_UVLO: held (0.3 V at most) is under its 0.776 V falling threshold, so RESET1 is released, R105 100 k lifts SYS_HOLD_G (D24
         BZT52C12, 11.4 to 12.7 V: Q43's VGS under its 20 V) and Q43 (2N7002, threshold 1 to 2.5 V) pulls RAIL_EN low (MAKER, INFERRED)
       RAIL_EN can reach the TPS62933's 1.1 V disable threshold only from VBAT 3.921 V up, where Q43's gate is 1.42 V over its 2.5 V threshold maximum; under
         U46's 2.7 V both outputs assert and Q43 is off, RAIL_EN then at most 0.758 V (MAKER, INFERRED)
     THE RESULT (INFERRED): the start ends at most 40.7 ms after VBAT begins to rise; the hold releases at least 78.6 ms after VBAT passes the rising
       threshold, 37.9 ms later at the least: no board A load on VSYS draws through the start; a quick undocking and redocking with VBAT held up:
       through board E's load: more than 37.8 mA takes VBAT under 8.309 V before the breaker can start (VSYS's 489 uF over 0.110 s), U46 asserts and the
       start is held; a smaller load leaves U42 on, and even stepped to U42's 1.802 A the breaker FET carries at most 22.1 W, under its 24.71 W least
       power limit, so its timer never runs
     PGD NOT USED (SESSION): it needs an eighth J_SMB position and a dock contact through two connectors from board P (record l8p); a supervisor
       on board A acts on what board A's loads see, for every start (a docking, the gauge's FET, a retry, a source-only rise), with no new interface
     the residuals (INFERRED):
       MAIN held through a docking: U1 asserts first and RAIL_EN follows the hold; the panel controller keeps at least 207.7 ms of U1's 400 ms KILL
         blanking to raise KILL; if it needs more, U1 releases EN and a second press starts the kit (E11-42 c)
       a source present: VSYS at 12.054 V at least holds U46 released, the loads stay on, and the breaker carries only what the charger does not, at
         4.764 V across its FET at most: under 4.53 A of excess its power limit never acts; over it the -1 latches (record l9stk 15.4b) while the
         source carries the kit, and 19h's inhibit keeps the charge off the latched FET
       a VBAT under 8.309 V in service holds every RAIL_EN converter and the dock branch (was each converter's own UVLO, about 4.3 V for U12): VBAT
         is at least the pack's 10.6 V less the path's drop or VSYS_MIN's 12.054 V in every mode, so only a collapse reaches it
       record l9stk's IF-5: once record l8p's drafts are applied the docking pulse E11-30 qualifies no longer arises; E11-30 is kept until then
     THE GUARANTEE UNDER THE -1 (record l9stk 15.4b: a start that meets the power limit latches and the kit stays dark; INFERRED):
       every start from a VBAT under 7.856 V (a docking, a redocking after the kit went dark, the input-return restart of 19h, the guard's cycle):
         no board A load draws (the hold outlasts the start by 37.9 ms at the least); the breaker FET carries the inrush alone, 11.1 W
       a start with VBAT held over 7.856 V by board A's capacitance (a quick redocking): at most 22.1 W, under the 24.71 W least power limit
       a start with a source carrying VSYS: at most 4.53 A of excess over the charger before the power limit acts; beyond that the pack
         latches while the source carries the kit, which stays up (not dark)
   19h. DD-7: THE LATCH-OFF -1, THE INPUT-RETURN RESET AND THE HARDWARE CHARGE INHIBIT (record l9stk 15.4b at d449375b; the checker's B-R2)
     the -1 (RECORD, l9stk): selected over the -2; after a trip it stays off until UVLO or VIN cycles; the timer falls under 0.3 V in 34.0 ms at
       most; UVLO falls under its threshold 1.097 ms after the loop opens; a restart within 0.633 s once the loop closes (the hold and the start)
     THE INPUT-RETURN RESET (SESSION, drafted in apply_gen_sch_a_dd7.py, after record l8p's PTC draft): Q44 (2N7002) pulls DOCK_EN_RET low,
       which opens the loop as an undocking does; its gate DD7_G is VIN_RAW through R106 1M, clamped by D25 (BZT52C12, 11.4 to 12.7 V);
       Q45 (gate FE_RUN) ends the pulse when U34 releases the front end, 78.6 / 127.3 / 201.2 ms after VIN_RAW passes U34's UV threshold (6.889 to 7.282 V
       rising with this record's R14), C212 being C105's part and value on the same TPS37A010122; Q46 (gate DD7_ALIVE, CELL+ over R107 /
       R108) holds the gate low while CELL+ is over 5.05 V, and cannot conduct under 1.98 V: an input arriving on a live pack opens nothing
       (MAKER, INFERRED)
     the pulse against what it must do (INFERRED): at least 78.6 ms, 72 times UVLO's 1.097 ms fall; the timer's 34.0 ms re-enable falls inside the
       pulse and the hold, 154.6 ms to spare; from VIN_RAW passing U34's threshold to the restart's end at most 0.835 s
     THE HARDWARE CHARGE INHIBIT (SESSION, the same draft; the checker's B-R2: a persistent fault latches the -1 again with the input still
       present and no second pulse comes): Q47 (gate SYS_INH_G, DOCK_EN_OUT over R109 1M and R144 1M) turns Q49 (AO3401A) on through R82
       100k and R83 200k; Q49 holds CH_BATDRV at VBAT, so Q39, Q40 and Q42 are off and their body diodes point from the pack to VSYS: no
       charge leaves VSYS for the pack; Q48 (gate DD7_ALIVE) releases it once CELL+ is over 5.05 V. The signal: the loop powered (DOCK_EN_OUT
       alive: the pack's cells reach board P's breaker) and the terminal dead (CELL+ under 1.98 V): exactly the breaker off (latched, in its
       hold or starting) with the cells present; no firmware (MAKER, INFERRED)
     its levels (INFERRED): DOCK_EN_OUT at least 7.735 V docked (the pack's 10.6 V, RT1 at its cold least 5 kOhm, l8p's 10 k and 22 k), SYS_INH_G at
       least 3.829 V over Q47's 2.5 V threshold maximum; Q49's VGS -4.07 V at VSYS_MIN's 12.054 V (threshold -1.3 V at most) and -9.86 V at the 29.2 V
       clamp (12 V absolute); BATDRV meanwhile sinks at most 3.83 mA (11.5 V over its 3 kOhm least RBATDRV_ON, SLUSE65A; MAKER, INFERRED)
     the loop's load (INFERRED, an interface effect for records l9stk and l8p): the 2 MOhm sense at DOCK_EN_OUT moves the first inverter's gate
       at l9stk's bound point (10.6 V, RT1 at 47 kOhm) from 2.952 V to 2.939 V, against its 2.5 V threshold
     not inhibited, by design: with the loop unpowered (the gauge's FETs off, a pack absent, undocked) a pack's wake and precharge pass the
       breaker's body diodes at the gauge's own current (record l9stk's charge direction); source-only operation (U-04) is untouched (RECORD)
     E-14, EXTENDED TO A SECOND LATCH WITH THE INPUT PRESENT (INFERRED): with the inhibit the charge into a latched breaker is the battery
       FETs' off leakage (IDSS 1 uA at 25 C each, the hot value not printed); without it, at the breaker FET's VSD 1 V at most and IF-2's 52.5 C/W:
         the charger's ChargeCurrent at POR (TI's E2E answer, D4), 0.256 A: 0.256 W, TJ 89.7 C held
         R-b's largest actual current, 0x0200 inside TI's row condition, 1.2567 A: 1.257 W, TJ 142.2 C held
       so the inhibit is what holds a commanded charge beyond R-b off the FET (the checker's 4 A, 4 W, 276 C); E11-45 measures it (INFERRED)
     the charger-side hold (SESSION): hardware, the inhibit above, until the terminal is alive; the firmware's IF-7 reports the trip and writes
       ChargeCurrent only after the restart (E11-44); the hold does not wait on it
     residuals (INFERRED): Q49 shorted holds the battery FETs off (their body diodes carry the discharge, and record l8p's PTC trips the breaker
       before their junctions pass 150 C); Q47, Q48 or Q49 open loses the inhibit or never releases it (both found by E11-45); a Q46 open lets
       an input's arrival drop a live pack for the pulse and the restart (E11-45 b); Q44 shorted holds the breaker off (fail-safe, revealed)
     STATUS: DD-7 DRAFTED (the reset for the first restart, the hardware inhibit for every later latch), CONDITIONAL on E11-45 and on
       TI's answer on BATDRV held at VSYS (Q-TI-17's addendum); IF-7 the firmware owner's (SESSION)

END. Desk arithmetic; nothing is measured. Drafts: apply_gen_sch_e_entry.py (the entry, 3c; J_DCIN's XT60-F, 19), apply_gen_sch_a_guard.py
(R14, 3f), apply_gen_sch_e_timer.py (C5 and C121, the alternative while the LM5069 stays), apply_gen_sch_a_charger.py (the BQ25730, its three
battery FETs, the dock's VSYS contact and the VSYS hold U46, 14, 15 and 19), apply_gen_sch_e_aux.py and apply_pcb_interfaces_dock.py (board E's VSYS feed, 15a); the
first round's apply_gen_sch_e_uvlo.py is withdrawn; the knee is a specification (3f); the interface and firmware texts are drafts for Layer 5
in the record. Software tests establish this record's own behaviour only.
